## The Excel model (what is in it, read 12-Oct-2026)
Sheets: Cover, Company Tearsheet, Annual Model, Annual Model Seg, **Fuso Financials**, Quarterly Model, DCF, Peer Analysis, Charts, FS Codes (+ 3 veryHidden LSEG sheets).
- `Fuso Financials` (built in the segment-analysis session) holds sourced segment history FY03/2020 to FY03/2026 (sales, OP, D&A, capex additions, assets), consensus FY03/2027 to FY03/2031, management guidance by segment, Life Science price/volume indices, a driver log, Q1 FY03/2027 data. Use it as a cross-check; company PDFs prevail.
- Useful cross-checks found: consensus capex FY03/2027 29,900 / FY03/2028 23,600 / FY03/2029 12,000 / FY03/2030 13,000 / FY03/2031 30,000 (million yen); consensus FY03/2027 sales 91.3 bn vs guidance 85.8 bn; consensus FY03/2031 OP 42.3 bn vs MTP target 36.0 bn.
- Known label error: row 93 calls the Q1 FY03/2027 extraordinary income a "gain on sale of fixed assets"; it is a **subsidy** (3,704m yen).
- Net income guidance rows 38-39 (19,200 vs 16,600): see Fase0 notes, "Open conflicts". Do not call either wrong without the TDnet notice.

## Working rules that saved time in this folder
1. Tag every number D / I / ND with file and page; FY labels as FY03/20XX.
2. For deck numbers use the bilingual PDF in Fase0 or render the page; never trust md chart text.
3. The yuho is the source for capex by segment, depreciation policy, customers, risks. Decks are the source for management framing.
4. Check which yuho/term a peer file really is before using it (the Fujimi "Yuho_61st-term" is FY03/2013).
